# Force LF endings on text files that run inside the Linux build
# container or get parsed by Linux tools regardless of the platform of
# the working tree.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true converts
# scripts to CRLF on disk, and bash inside the Docker image fails on
# the first set/source/etc. line with errors like
# `set: -o: invalid option`.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
